  "story": {
    "day": 77,
    "title": "Kaya's Busy Morning",
    "sentences": [
      "One morning, Kaya had to get up at six.",
      "She put on her purple T-shirt and pants; mine were clean.",
      "Her other clothes, hers, were dirty. Her pet bird sang.",
      "Today, Kaya had track and field practice. She did not need a racket.",
      "The captain would talk to them; these people were kind.",
      "They sometimes ate a radish for custom.",
      "Kaya remembered Christmas in California. The beach was lovely.",
      "She took a photo there. It was a different place. She would try to speak.",
      "It was seven, then eight, then nine o'clock.",
      "The evening practice had ten players. One played a trumpet.",
      "It was a national sport. She sent her regards. Theirs was a good club.",
      "Kaya thought of a happy god."
    ]
  }
}